we need to find $x$ in terms of $y$ and $z.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=2y-3z-2 \\\\ y=y \\\\ z=z,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ and $z$ (the free variables) are arbitrary numbers.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2y-3z-2 \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -8 & 12 & -8 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -6 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -8 & 12 & -8 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -6 & 4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -8 & 12 & -8 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -6 & 4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -6 & 4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-2y+3z=-2 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z=0 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any numbers $x,y,z$ form a solution of the final two equations, we can remove these equations from the system. \n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is $x$, and we have two free variables, $y,$ and $z.$ That means we need to find $x$ in terms of $y$ and $z.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=2y-3z-2 \\\\ y=y \\\\ z=z,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ and $z$ (the free variables) are arbitrary numbers.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2y-3z-2 \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186400620 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2-2y+3z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" "\\begin{bmatrix}2-2y+3z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] [:db/cas 17592186400621 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2y-3z-2 \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" "\\begin{bmatrix}2y-3z-2 \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] [:db/cas 17592186400623 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}y-2z-1 \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" "\\begin{bmatrix}y-2z-1 \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] [:db/cas 17592186400624 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2y+3z+2 \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" "\\begin{bmatrix}2y+3z+2 \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] [:db/cas 17592186400625 :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 8 & -6 \\\\ -4 & -16 & 12 \\\\ 6 & 24 & -18\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 8 & -6 \\\\ -4 & -16 & 12 \\\\ 6 & 24 & -18\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -3 \\\\ -4 & -16 & 12 \\\\ 6 & 24 & -18\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 24 & -18\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-6{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now  \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+4y=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is $x$ and we have one free variable, $y.$ That means we need to find $x$  in terms of $y.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-4y-3 \\\\ y=y,\\